    "description": "Take a Herdr terminal address with letters, such as t1j\n\n## Summary\n\nThe orchestrator launcher rejected a Herdr terminal address that has letters in it, such as `t1j`. Herdr gives such addresses, so a start opened the tab and then failed with no output, and stop and focus said the handle was unknown. The launcher now takes each local Herdr address: the letter `t`, then letters and digits.\n\nCloses jerridan/crew#180\n\n**Ticket:** N/A — answers [issue 180](https://github.com/jerridan/crew/issues/180)\n**Type:** Bug fix\n\n---\n\n## Agent context\n\n### Authority\n\n- `docs/design.md` §15.153 (Herdr support) and the new §15.156 (this finding).\n- `skills/orchestrator/references/launcher.md` owns the launcher interface and the handle.\n\n### What changed, by file\n\n- `skills/orchestrator/scripts/launcher.py` — `HERDR_ID_RE` is now `t[0-9A-Za-z]+`. `start`, `resume`, `herdr_ttys()` (used by `find`, `resume` and the target check of `stop`) and `split_handle()` (used by `stop` and `focus`) all use it.\n- `skills/orchestrator/scripts/test-launcher.sh` — the `herdr-app` stub prints the address in `herdr-new-terminal` when that file exists. New checks: `start` with `t1j`, `focus herdr:t1j`, `find` of `t1j` and `t1B`, `stop herdr:t1j --name`, and four handles that `focus` still rejects (`herdr:t`, `herdr:x1j`, `herdr:t1-j`, `herdr:m/t7`).\n- `skills/orchestrator/references/launcher.md` — the Herdr term table states the address rule.\n- `docs/design.md` — finding §15.156.\n- `.claude-plugin/plugin.json`, `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` — version 0.1.124.\n\n### Constraints that applied\n\n- The issue says the pattern must follow the Herdr docs. `hc --help` says an address is \"like t7 or t1b\", and `hc get --help` names `machine/t7` for another machine. `hc --skill` and `hc schema` give no closer rule. So the pattern takes `t` and any letters and digits, and not the `machine/` form, because the launcher opens tabs on this machine only.\n- A change under `skills/` bumps the version in both manifests, to equal values.\n\n### How this was verified\n\n- The red commit `d8be5e5` ran `test-launcher.sh`: 300 of 305 checks passed, and the 5 new address checks failed.\n- After the fix: 305 of 305 checks passed.\n\n### Known gaps\n\nNo live run has started, found, focused or stopped a Herdr terminal with a letter address. Only the stubs give `t1j`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XrBTZeaaVuTzjnPwFcKrYa\n",
